{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484646-how-come-they-butchered-the-nararaja-path-disciplie-and-nobody-said-a-thing","id":1484646,"title":"How come they butchered the Nararaja Path/Disciplie and nobody said a thing!?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-21T13:59:15-07:00","id":1484646,"title":"How come they butchered the Nararaja Path/Disciplie and nobody said a thing!?","content":"I'm appalled to find this out now. I was by chance rereading VDAV20 some moments ago when I came upon the Nararaja path, more specifically the <i>Vitreous Path</i>. Am I reading it right, or does the level 4 and 5 now only cause 1(1!?) Aggravated damage if used for attack (the other level 4 application is to summon spectres to &quot;make boo and nothing else&quot;, so I'd rather ignore it for now lol))!? One of my players asked if it meant 1 per success, but by the text it states only 1. I mean, how can a level 4 power cause 1 level of aggravated damage? Somebody please confirm it was just a mistake and it's supposed to be 1 per success. Even though I'm definitely no big fan of the Nagaraja, far from it (And this comes from a &quot;fan&quot; of the Tal'Mahe'Ra, but this is a topic for another thread...), I feel this is a bit too much, isn't it? Their old level 4 of Nihililistics caused 2 damage per success, it was good. I loved the idea that they made it a path, because it makes little sense for it to be another discipline, but at the very least I expected them to keep the powers in the same level, not to completely butcher it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T14:50:45-07:00","id":1484652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484646-how-come-they-butchered-the-nararaja-path-disciplie-and-nobody-said-a-thing#post1484646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm appalled to find this out now. I was by chance rereading VDAV20 some moments ago when I came upon the Nararaja path, more specifically the <i>Vitreous Path</i>. Am I reading it right, or does the level 4 and 5 now only cause 1(1!?) Aggravated damage if used for attack (the other level 4 application is to summon spectres to &quot;make boo and nothing else&quot;, so I'd rather ignore it for now lol))!? One of my players asked if it meant 1 per success, but by the text it states only 1. I mean, how can a level 4 power cause 1 level of aggravated damage? Somebody please confirm it was just a mistake and it's supposed to be 1 per success. Even though I'm definitely no big fan of the Nagaraja, far from it (And this comes from a &quot;fan&quot; of the Tal'Mahe'Ra, but this is a topic for another thread...), I feel this is a bit too much, isn't it? Their old level 4 of Nihililistics caused 2 damage per success, it was good. I loved the idea that they made it a path, because it makes little sense for it to be another discipline, but at the very least I expected them to keep the powers in the same level, not to completely butcher it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would guess it's a mistake, but to be fair i don't use Nagaraja much in my games - and when i do, <i>never</i> under that particular name (&quot;serpent monarch&quot;), that in my games i reserve for the most respected elders of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shesha\" target=\"_blank\">Followers of Shesha</a> clan in India.<br /> <br /> The necromantic bloodline from DSotBH i call Hungry Ghosts, Preta and a number of other things instead, specially in Asia - and might or not have some elusive connection to the Cappadocians (long before he Hecata mash up from V5).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-21-2022, 05:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T15:18:00-07:00","id":1484656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484646-how-come-they-butchered-the-nararaja-path-disciplie-and-nobody-said-a-thing?p=1484652#post1484652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would guess it's a mistake, but to be fair i don't use Nagaraja much in my games - and when i do, <i>never</i> under that particular name (&quot;serpent monarch&quot;), that in my games i reserve for the most respected elders of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shesha\" target=\"_blank\">Followers of Shesha</a> clan in India.<br /> <br /> The necromantic bloodline from DSotBH i call Hungry Ghosts, Preta and a number of other things instead, specially in Asia - and might or not have some elusive connection to the Cappadocians (long before he Hecata mash up from V5).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the reply. It's great to know that another person also think it's a mistake as no sane mind could ever think that causing 1 level of aggravated damage is worth a level 1 path, let alone a 4/5. By the way, I, for some reason also hate the name of the bloodline, I think I'm gonna rename them as well, if players keep asking me to play as a Nagaraja I'm going to tell them the bloodline has another name in my game (I just need to figure out which name to choose<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T15:21:07-07:00","id":1484657,"title":"","content":"Oh and also, the idea to make them having a connection to the Cappadocian is a very good one. I can't really get myself to like the &quot;&quot;original&quot;&quot; idea of how they came into beings, I'd prefer them to have some connection to the clan of death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T21:08:10-07:00","id":1484668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484646-how-come-they-butchered-the-nararaja-path-disciplie-and-nobody-said-a-thing?p=1484656#post1484656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thanks for the reply. It's great to know that another person also think it's a mistake as no sane mind could ever think that causing 1 level of aggravated damage is worth a level 1 path, let alone a 4/5. By the way, I, for some reason also hate the name of the bloodline, I think I'm gonna rename them as well, if players keep asking me to play as a Nagaraja I'm going to tell them the bloodline has another name in my game (I just need to figure out which name to choose<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As i mentioned previously, in my games they are known under a variety of names instead of just one - a lack of clear recognition or unified identity that many in kindred society see as clear indicator of a bloodline, a false clan made of pretensions, possibly spawned of those rejected from their clans for tainting their blood, caitiffs or worse.<br /> In fact &quot;Nihililistics&quot; is the name by which kindred of this line/cult in the West (mainly germany, austria, russia and some parts of central-eastern europe) and sometimes confused with Lasombra Abyss Mystics.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484646-how-come-they-butchered-the-nararaja-path-disciplie-and-nobody-said-a-thing?p=1484657#post1484657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh and also, the idea to make them having a connection to the Cappadocian is a very good one. I can't really get myself to like the &quot;&quot;original&quot;&quot; idea of how they came into beings, I'd prefer them to have some connection to the clan of death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Me, i muddy things a bit - they may be a remnant branch of the Capadocians or even Lamia, the blood cult/revenant lineage of an ancient of that clan that perpetrated strange feats of death magic in an attempt at preserving their nature after the loss of their master or mistress.<br /> <br /> Or maybe the cultists outright devoured their undead master in a misguided attempt to replicate the empowerment through embrace or diablerie and things went extra pear-shaped because the corpse of one versed in Mortis/Mortuus path can be peculiarly durable in strange ways.<br /> <br /> Or it was no accident or betrayal at all and that elusive ancient abides still, as a guide and secret passenger within each ot its bastardized blood descendants.<br /> <br /> Many possibilities, rumors and crack theories abound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-22-2022, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T22:20:42-07:00","id":1484670,"title":"","content":"DAV20 is a clusterfuck largely because it was mostly given to freelancers with little oversight. Some of it's fantastic as a result, more often it's offensively garbage. Compared to the abominable changes to the Assamites, the Nagaraja can fly under the radar no problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T11:54:11-07:00","id":1484788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484646-how-come-they-butchered-the-nararaja-path-disciplie-and-nobody-said-a-thing?p=1484670#post1484670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> DAV20 is a clusterfuck largely because it was mostly given to freelancers with little oversight. Some of it's fantastic as a result, more often it's offensively garbage. Compared to the abominable changes to the Assamites, the Nagaraja can fly under the radar no problem.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What &quot;abominable changes to the Assamites&quot; you mean, exactly (that just made me curious)? Overall I agree that the book, while having many interesting things and being very beautiful, has some weird things and mistakes like the one I mentioned (and some shitty powers like &quot;Armored Flesh&quot; that enrages me).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T12:53:34-07:00","id":1484796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484646-how-come-they-butchered-the-nararaja-path-disciplie-and-nobody-said-a-thing?p=1484788#post1484788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What &quot;abominable changes to the Assamites&quot; you mean, exactly (that just made me curious)? Overall I agree that the book, while having many interesting things and being very beautiful, has some weird things and mistakes like the one I mentioned (and some shitty powers like &quot;Armored Flesh&quot; that enrages me).</div> </div> </div> </div>The first level of Quietus (the warrior branch) allows you to turn hearts into little potions so that you can save them for later. Remember how assamites were supposed to be moving away from just being one-note psychopaths? This certainly ain't the way to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T13:27:48-07:00","id":1484802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484646-how-come-they-butchered-the-nararaja-path-disciplie-and-nobody-said-a-thing?p=1484796#post1484796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first level of Quietus (the warrior branch) allows you to turn hearts into little potions so that you can save them for later. Remember how assamites were supposed to be moving away from just being one-note psychopaths? This certainly ain't the way to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh sure! I certainly didn't understand why change the &quot;Silence Power&quot; of Quietus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-25T21:25:47-07:00","id":1485008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484646-how-come-they-butchered-the-nararaja-path-disciplie-and-nobody-said-a-thing?p=1484796#post1484796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first level of Quietus (the warrior branch) allows you to turn hearts into little potions so that you can save them for later. Remember how assamites were supposed to be moving away from just being one-note psychopaths? This certainly ain't the way to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I just chalk that up to the notion that NOW they\u2019re moving away from being one-note paychopaths\u2026 but back THEN they were indeed one-note psychos.<br /> <br /> Personally, I only run/play modern era games, but appreciate the slightly flashier options of DAV20 (particularly for combat rules). So if there are different powers between V20 and DAV20 I just allow the player to pick whichever one makes sense for their character (with the exception of the three physical disciplines which use DAV20 because I also use DAV20\u2019s combat rules). As such, the discipline difference means Assamites get another choice for that level rather than being locked into just one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-26T15:12:38-07:00","id":1485059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1484646-how-come-they-butchered-the-nararaja-path-disciplie-and-nobody-said-a-thing?p=1484796#post1484796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first level of Quietus (the warrior branch) allows you to turn hearts into little potions so that you can save them for later. Remember how assamites were supposed to be moving away from just being one-note psychopaths? This certainly ain't the way to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>My issue with this change was that it made a power that was presumably for all Assamites - of all castes - too much like blood sorcery. It sounds more like a Ritual than a native part of the Clan's kit.<br /> <br /> Especially weird, since DAV20 positioned the Vizier caste as being the &quot;vanilla&quot; Assamites. What are scholars, artisans, and diplomats doing with that kind of power?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-27T12:50:25-07:00","id":1485132,"title":"","content":"So umm..Dark Ages: Vampire Quietus level 5 is blood essence. Its not new, they just moved it the first level instead of level 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T08:31:15-07:00","id":1485379,"title":"","content":"My first guess, before reading the entry in V20DA, was that it was 'one damage' in the way an attack with a knife is only 'Str+1'. So, it would be 1 + successes. <br /> <br /> But on reading the rules for Curse of the Maelstrom (Vitreous Path 4), it seems the damage is almost beside the point. The point is to mark your target as blighted for a night, thus making social attempts harder. It's pretty naff for a four-dot power, but I don't think it's an error.<br /> <br /> A simple fix to make it more powerful would be to have that power inflict the Haunted Flaw on a location or individual for one night per success. Nice and easy, feels in-keeping with the intent, and doesn't leave things as vague as the RAW. The main difference is that your ghostly stalker is a spectre, so much more aggressive than usual, but the Flaw would otherwise cover it.<br /> <br /> Something more flavoursome would be for it to reduce a target's Appearance by one dot per success, which can only be healed as aggravated damage. It has a strong social and roleplaying effect but isn't lethal nor is it OP at level four.<br /> <br /> As for Night Call (Vitreous Path 5), the rules seem even weaker here, and I'd be tempted to say it's '1 + successes' for the offensive use. With that being aggravated damage, that's a satisfactory effect, though a bland one.<br /> <br /> But you could have it add a Flaw like Hand of Hades instead (the exaggerated version of Touch of Frost, which withers plants and slowly sucks the life out of those around you). The duration would be one night per success again.<br /> <br /> The thing with V20DA is that some powers are much, much stronger, or better detailed, while others are pretty weak or missing key details. <br /> <br /> For example, as written, Night Cry has no duration listed for the difficulty reduction. So does the modifier apply for a turn? 'All actions' implies multiple actions, so probably not a turn. So is that a night? A chapter? A story? <br /> <br /> Likewise, Curse of the Maelstrom has a duration when you target an individual, but not for generally invoking spectres (I assume it's supposed to be until sunrise too). It could have done with another editing pass.<br /> <br /> Generally, though, I like most of the Discipline changes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T08:51:19-07:00","id":1485382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Generally, though, I like most of the Discipline changes. </div> </div> </div>Me too, but there are many &quot;holes&quot; in there. The Nagaraja's Vitreous Path is one of these, I prefer to keep with the original and completely ignore the BS they made in DAV20. But you're right that in most cases it did a good job (like with Temporis).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}